in statistical mechanics. The subcritical bifurcation is sometimes called an inverted or backward bifurcation, and is related to discontinuous or first-order phase transitions. In the engineering literature, the supercritical bifurcation is sometimes called soft or safe, because the nonzero fixed points are born at small amplitude; in contrast, the subcritical bifurcation is hard or dangerous, because of the jump from zero to large amplitude.
